## Why This Is Asked

Tests end-to-end exactly-once thinking across DB, Kafka, and Redis in high-throughput CNPA.

## Key Concepts

- Idempotency keys
- Outbox pattern
- Kafka transactions
- Redis cache invalidation
- Dedup store and replay protection
- Observability and load testing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo transactional flow for exactly-once
// 1) write to outbox atomically with main write
db.insertOutbox(eventId, payload, false);
db.commitTransaction();

// 2) publish via Kafka using transactions
producer.initTransactions();
producer.beginTransaction();
producer.send({ topic: 'events', key: eventId, value: payload });
producer.commitTransaction();

// 3) mark outbox as published and invalidate cache
db.markOutboxPublished(eventId);
db.commitTransaction();
redis.invalidate(eventId);
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate end-to-end exactly-once under load and define guardrails for replay?
- What metrics and rollback criteria would you use to detect and recover from dedup store growth or Kafka transaction failures?
